      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُ أَبَا اَلْحَسَنِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ قَالَ لِمَمْلُوكِهِ أَنْتَ حُرٌّ وَ لِي مَالُكَ قَالَ \"يَبْدَأُ بِالْمَالِ قَبْلَ اَلْعِتْقِ يَقُولُ لِي مَالُكَ وَ أَنْتَ حُرٌّ بِرِضاً مِنَ اَلْمَمْلُوكِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3557 - Sa'd ibn Sa'd narrated from Hariz who said:\nI asked Abu al-Hasan (as) about a man who said to his slave, \"You are free, and your wealth belongs to me.\"\nImam (as) said: \"He must begin with the wealth before granting freedom, saying, 'Your wealth belongs to me, and you are free,' with the consent of the slave.\""
        ]
      }
